 -- Bibliograph Maintainers <maintainers@olamaelcu.net>  Sat, 07 Nov 2026 08:00:32 -0500

bibliograph (0.5.10) unstable; urgency=medium

  * `community.lexicon.book.searchEditions` is a query again. It was a query
    until 0.5.9's canonical-identifier work moved it to a procedure to carry
    structured `identifiers`; a search is a read, so it must be cacheable and
    idempotent per the XRPC spec, and clients that GET it were answered with
    405. The hints now travel as parameters — `q`, `title`, `author`,
    `identifiers` (each `<type>:<value>`, the canonical pair encoded as one
    string) — with `offset`/`limit` paging, and the handler parses the pairs.
  * The compatibility endpoint advertises it as a query again.
  * The description backfill runs hourly instead of daily: one 1,000-row batch
    at :40 of every hour (~24k/day, keeping the daily volume near the previous
    20k) so the 232k-row backlog drains steadily without exceeding the shared
    Google Books quota. The ISBN (00:25) and cover (even hours, :00) ticks keep
    their offsets, so the three scans do not race each other.

