bibliograph (0.2.7) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Cover bytes from Google Books and Open Library are cached on disk. The
    `getImageForBook` response now points at `/image/cover`, which fetches an
    allowlisted provider URL once, writes it under `COVER_CACHE_DIR`, and
    serves later readers from disk. Concurrent misses share one upstream
    request; redirects are followed only within the provider allowlist.
  * The Debian unit provisions `/var/lib/bibliograph/covers` through
    `StateDirectory=` so the cache survives upgrades, and the conffile documents
    the path.

