bibliograph (0.2.6) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The `net.olamaelcu.livtet.biblio.graph.follow` procedure is gone, along with
    the `follows` table it wrote. Its purpose was to keep a local copy of the
    follow graph for the social feeds, but nothing read it: 0.2.5 made those
    feeds read `net.olamaelcu.livtet.biblio.follow` records from the reader's
    own repo. Following and unfollowing are now purely a PDS write from the
    client; there is no Bibliograph-side index to keep in step.
  * `0022_drop_follows` drops the table. Combined with `0021_follows`, which
    created it, the pair is idempotent: an environment that never applied either
    still ends up without the table.

